jobDescription:
Job Description
We are building the agent platform behind our consumer assistant. You will:
1. Design and operate backend services for LLM-powered agents: tool routing, memory storage, session state, and rate limiting;
2. Own reliability of the inference gateway (retries, timeouts, fallbacks across model providers) and its observability (tracing, cost accounting, regression detection);
3. Build evaluation pipelines that replay production traces against new prompts and models before rollout;
4. Collaborate with applied research to ship RAG and structured-output features to production.
Requirements
1. BS/MS in Computer Science or equivalent; 1+ years of backend experience or strong internship/project record;
2. Proficient in Go, Python, or TypeScript; solid understanding of HTTP, queues, caches and relational databases;
3. Hands-on experience with LLM APIs, prompt engineering, function calling or MCP; familiarity with LangChain/LangGraph is a plus;
4. Comfortable using AI coding tools (Cursor, Claude Code, Codex) in daily work;
5. Clear written communication; ownership mindset.
